1
00:00:02,120 --> 00:00:07,200
If they worked hard, at least they worked for themselves.

2
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:10,920
No creature among them went upon two legs.

3
00:00:10,920 --> 00:00:15,799
No creature called any other creature master.

4
00:00:15,799 --> 00:00:19,799
All animals were equal.

5
00:00:19,840 --> 00:00:24,000
One day in early summer, Squealer ordered the sheep to follow him and led

6
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:27,639
them out to a piece of waste ground at the other end of the farm, which had

7
00:00:27,639 --> 00:00:31,280
become overgrown with birch saplings.

8
00:00:31,280 --> 00:00:37,040
The sheep spent the whole day there browsing at the leaves under Squealer's supervision.

9
00:00:37,040 --> 00:00:41,639
In the evening, he returned to the farmhouse himself, but as it was warm

10
00:00:41,639 --> 00:00:45,319
weather, told the sheep to stay where they were.

11
00:00:45,319 --> 00:00:50,399
It ended by their remaining there for a whole week, during which time the other

12
00:00:50,399 --> 00:00:53,399
animals saw nothing of them.

13
00:00:53,399 --> 00:00:57,440
Squealer was with them for the greater part of every day.

14
00:00:57,440 --> 00:01:04,200
He was, he said, teaching them to sing a new song for which privacy was needed.

15
00:01:04,200 --> 00:01:08,319
It was just after the sheep had returned on a pleasant evening when the animals

16
00:01:08,319 --> 00:01:12,639
had finished work and were making their way back to the farm buildings,

17
00:01:12,639 --> 00:01:17,040
that the terrified neighing of a horse sounded from the yard.

18
00:01:17,040 --> 00:01:20,639
Startled, the animals stopped in their tracks.

19
00:01:20,639 --> 00:01:22,760
It was Clover's voice.

20
00:01:22,760 --> 00:01:29,000
She neighed again, and all the animals broke into a gallop and rushed into the yard.

21
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:32,360
Then, they saw what Clover had seen.

22
00:01:32,360 --> 00:01:36,120
It was a pig walking on his hind legs.

23
00:01:36,120 --> 00:01:38,680
Yes, it was Squealer.

24
00:01:38,680 --> 00:01:43,159
A little awkwardly, as though not quite used to supporting his considerable bulk

25
00:01:43,159 --> 00:01:48,520
in that position, but with perfect balance, he was strolling across the yard.

26
00:01:48,520 --> 00:01:54,000
And a moment later, out from the door of the farmhouse came a long file of pigs,

27
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:57,120
all walking on their hind legs.

28
00:01:57,120 --> 00:02:02,239
Some did it better than others. One or two were even a trifle unsteady and

29
00:02:02,239 --> 00:02:06,040
looked as though they would have liked the support of a stick, but every one of

30
00:02:06,040 --> 00:02:10,200
them made his way right round the yard successfully.

31
00:02:10,200 --> 00:02:15,319
And finally, there was a tremendous baying of dogs and a shrill crowing from

32
00:02:15,319 --> 00:02:21,000
the black cockerel, and out came Napoleon himself, majestically upright,

33
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:27,840
casting haughty glances from side to side, and with his dogs gambling round him.

34
00:02:27,840 --> 00:02:30,600
He carried a whip in his trotter.

35
00:02:30,600 --> 00:02:33,239
There was a deadly silence.

36
00:02:33,239 --> 00:02:39,000
Amazed, terrified, huddling together, the animals watched the long line of

37
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:42,280
pigs march slowly round the yard.

38
00:02:42,280 --> 00:02:46,680
It was as though the world had turned upside down.

39
00:02:46,680 --> 00:02:51,639
Then there came a moment when the first shock had worn off, and when, in spite

40
00:02:51,639 --> 00:02:56,680
of everything, in spite of their terror of the dogs and of the habit developed

41
00:02:56,680 --> 00:03:03,000
through long years of never complaining, never criticizing, no matter what happened,

42
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:06,680
They might have uttered some word of protest.

43
00:03:06,680 --> 00:03:12,079
But just at that moment, as though at a signal, all the sheep burst out into a

44
00:03:12,079 --> 00:03:17,280
tremendous bleating of "Four legs good, two legs better.

45
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:20,040
Four legs good, two legs better.

46
00:03:20,040 --> 00:03:24,280
Four legs good, two legs better."

47
00:03:24,600 --> 00:03:27,799
It went on for 5 minutes without stopping.

48
00:03:27,799 --> 00:03:33,760
And by the time the sheep had quieted down, the chance to utter any protest had passed.

49
00:03:33,760 --> 00:03:37,959
For the pigs had marched back into the farmhouse.

50
00:03:37,959 --> 00:03:41,520
Benjamin felt a nose nuzzling at his shoulder.

51
00:03:41,520 --> 00:03:43,000
He looked round.

52
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:44,000
It was Clover.
